{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If in My statutes you walk.</b> Might this be the fulfillment of the commandments? When it says ״וְאֶת מִצְוֹתַי תִּשְׁמְרוּ וַעֲשִיתֶם אֹתָם״ — fulfillment of the commandments is already stated. So what do I establish by ״אִם בְּחֻקֹּתַי תֵּלֵכוּ״? That you toil in Torah (Sifra)." "<b>And My commandments you shall keep.</b> Toil in Torah on condition to keep and to fulfill, as it says ״וּלְמַדְתֶּם אֹתָם וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם לַעֲשֹׂתָם״ (Deuteronomy 5)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:33.802063776Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}